UPDATE companies SET description='Pascagoula Sheet Metal Works operates from Pascagoula, Mississippi, on the Gulf Coast. The business traces its roots to 1944 when Lawrence Hill and his sons established Lawrence Hill and Sons Roofing and Sheet Metal. The company was incorporated under its current name in 1967 and has remained family‑owned and operated for three generations; it is now woman‑owned and operated.

The shop specializes in custom sheet metal fabrication for industrial customers. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

Primary customers are industrial firms along the Mississippi Gulf Coast, with a notable presence in the marine sector. Concrete examples from the company’s own project photos include a stainless‑steel motor shroud remake, marine duct fabricated to fit confined areas, a vortex breaker, and an aluminum filter rack housing.

The company highlights its multi‑generational family ownership and recent transition to woman‑owned leadership as key differentiators, emphasizing long‑term local service and custom fabrication expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Perforating", "Marine duct fabrication", "Vortex breaker fabrication", "Aluminum filter rack housing fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Marine"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Sheet metal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated for three generations", "Woman-owned and operated", "Custom sheet metal fabrication for industrial sector", "Perforating capability", "Serving Mississippi Gulf Coast since 1944"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1944 as Lawrence Hill and Sons Roofing and Sheet Metal -> /about-us", "Incorporated as Pascagoula Sheet Metal Works in 1967 -> /about-us", "Family-owned for three generations, now woman-owned -> /about-us", "Location: 5609 Veteran''s St., Pascagoula, MS 39581 -> / and /about-us", "Specializes in custom sheet metal fabrication for industrial sector -> /about-us", "Capability to perforate material as needed -> / and /about-us", "Examples: motor shroud remade into stainless steel, marine duct, vortex breaker, aluminum filter rack housing -> / and /about-us", "Serving Mississippi Gulf Coast for over 50 years -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Pascagoula Sheet Metal specializes in custom sheet metal fabrication in the industrial sector for the Mississippi Gulf Coast.", "founded_year": "1944", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pascagoula-sheet-metal-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Patriot Equipment, headquartered in Minden, Nebraska, traces its roots to 1984 when Harold Lempka opened Minden Machine Shop in a 30-by-50-foot building along the railroad tracks. Initially a side venture with a partner, the shop repaired and built machinery using an old lathe and welder. After the partner departed, Harold''s sons Larry and Kerry joined the business, and the operation transitioned from contract machining to manufacturing its own line of farm equipment.

Today the company operates across more than 92,000 square feet of production space with a workforce exceeding 60 people. It manufactures and sells 31 distinct equipment lines—seed tenders alone offer ten size and style variations—while maintaining a job-shop division that handles custom fabrication and repair work in steel, stainless steel, and aluminum. Capabilities include laser cutting, robotic and hand welding, bending, sawing, painting, assembly, and hydraulic and electrical integration.

The primary customer base is agricultural producers, but the shop also serves commercial firms, schools, and hospitals that require custom metalwork or equipment repairs. Products are sold directly and through a dealer network across the United States.

The business was built on a simple principle articulated by Harold Lempka: do a good job at a fair price and treat the customer with respect. That philosophy, combined with a deep sense of patriotism that inspired the Patriot Equipment brand in 1994, continues to guide the company''s growth.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Drafting", "Advanced Laser Cutting", "Metal Bending", "Material Sawing", "Robotic Welding", "Hand Welding", "Painting", "Router Table Cutting", "Assembly Work", "Electrical", "Small Engine", "Large Engine", "Hydraulics"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Commercial", "Education", "Healthcare"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 by Harold Lempka -> /about-us", "Started in 30x50 ft building -> /about-us", "Sons Larry and Kerry joined -> /about-us", "Branded Patriot Equipment 1994 -> /about-us", "Moved to current location 1995 -> /about-us", "Employee counts: 19 (2004), 30 (2008), now >60 -> /about-us", "Facility >92,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "31 equipment lines, seed tenders 10 variations -> /about-us", "Machine shop repairs for farmers, companies, schools, hospitals -> /about-us", "Philosophy: good job at fair price, treat customer with respect -> /about-us", "Capabilities: Drafting, Laser Cutting, Bending, Sawing, Robotic/Hand Welding, Painting, Router Cutting, Assembly, Electrical, Engines, Hydraulics -> /services", "Materials: Steel, Stainless Steel, Aluminum -> /services", "Headquarters: Minden, Nebraska -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Patriot Equipment manufactures and sells 31 lines of equipment", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "60+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='patriot-equipment-minden-machine-shop-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Patton Electronics Co., operating as Patton LLC, is headquartered in Gaithersburg, Maryland. The company describes itself as a multi-national organization with global offices in the United States, Hungary, and Switzerland, though its founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed on its website.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures network access, connectivity, voice-over-IP, high-availability, triple-play, and video surveillance equipment for carrier, enterprise, and industrial networks. Its capabilities span embedded system design—including hardware definition, software architecture, and verification—through project management and original design manufacturing and distribution (ODMD). Patton emphasizes a flexible production model with a minimum order quantity as low as one unit and the ability to ramp to large-volume production.

Patton serves defense, telecommunications, broadcast, and critical-infrastructure sectors. Recent projects include a subcontract to develop source-secure fiber optic modules for U.S. defense applications, a partnership with alfanar to accelerate secure digital transformation of Saudi power infrastructure, and collaboration with Artel on carrier-class PTP switches for modern broadcast. The company also supplies Tone Commander secure SIP phones with JITC/STIG certifications and NSA-listed data diode kits for critical infrastructure protection.

Patton differentiates itself through U.S.-manufactured network equipment, a full-spectrum embedded solutions capability from feasibility to acceptance, and an ODMD model that allows customers to brand Patton-designed hardware. The firm also highlights its global support infrastructure offering Level 1, 2, and 3 support tiers.', certifications=ARRAY['JITC/STIG','NSA-listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Embedded system design and development", "Hardware definition and development", "Software architecture and development", "Verification, commissioning and acceptance", "Project management and program management", "Feasibility and cost analysis", "ODMD (Original Design, Manufacturing and Distribution)", "Network access equipment manufacturing", "VoIP equipment manufacturing", "Video surveillance equipment manufacturing", "Fiber optic module development", "Data diode kit manufacturing", "12G-SDI fiber extender manufacturing", "Industrial Ethernet switch manufacturing", "PoE extender manufacturing", "xDSL modem manufacturing", "Media gateway manufacturing", "Session border controller manufacturing", "SFP module manufacturing", "Fiber telecom equipment manufacturing (T1/E1/PRI, Analog & ISDN)", "Serial data communication over fiber", "Ethernet over fiber transport", "Video over IP transport", "Video over fiber transport"], "industries": ["Defense/Security", "Telecommunications", "Broadcast/Media", "Critical Infrastructure", "Industrial Networks", "Carrier Networks", "Enterprise Networks", "Power/Utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to large-volume production; minimum order quantity as low as 1 unit; estimated annual usage in the 100s", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S.-manufactured network equipment", "Minimum order quantity as low as 1 unit", "ODMD (Original Design, Manufacturing and Distribution) model", "Complete embedded system capabilities from feasibility through acceptance", "Global Level 1/2/3 support infrastructure"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Gaithersburg, Maryland -> db", "Multi-national organization with global offices in US, Hungary, Switzerland -> /capabilities, /", "Designs, develops, manufactures network access, VoIP, video surveillance equipment -> /capabilities", "Embedded system capabilities: hardware, software, verification -> /capabilities", "Project management and program management solutions -> /capabilities", "ODMD model with MOQ as low as 1 unit -> /capabilities", "US-manufactured network equipment -> /", "Defense subcontract for source-secure fiber optic modules -> /", "Partnership with alfanar for Saudi power infrastructure -> /", "Collaboration with Artel on broadcast PTP switches -> /", "Tone Commander SIP phones with JITC/STIG certifications -> /", "NSA-listed data diode kit for critical infrastructure -> /", "12G-SDI fiber extender kits manufactured in US -> /", "Global support Level 1/2/3 -> /capabilities", "Industries: defense, telecom, broadcast, critical infrastructure, industrial, carrier, enterprise -> /capabilities, /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Patton is a multi-national organization that designs, develops, and manufactures network access, connectivity, voice-over-IP, high availability, triple play, and video surveillance equipment", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 unit", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='patton-electronics-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Patton''s Medical is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina. The company traces its roots to Pattons Inc., which began selling custom medical air packages to hospitals in 1980. In 2008, the leadership created Patton''s Medical to sell and service their own medical gas equipment nationwide. Since 2012, the business has been owned and operated by ELGi USA, which acquired Pattons Inc. and Patton''s Medical as an entry into the U.S. medical equipment market.

The company designs, assembles, and services medical air systems built around Hitachi oil-less reciprocating scroll compressors (available in base-mount, modular, and tank-mounted configurations) and medical vacuum systems that use Busch oil-less, contactless multi-claw technology. It also supplies pipeline products — including fully automatic universal medical manifolds, outlets, zone valves, alarms, and architectural products — through strategic partnerships. Control panels are built to UL 508A standards, and all equipment is designed to meet or exceed NFPA 99 requirements. The firm offers custom package engineering for unique facility specifications and provides installation and ongoing service across the country.

Patton''s Medical serves hospitals, clinical laboratories, and university research facilities that require compliant medical gas and laboratory air systems.

The business was started to move beyond distribution and offer proprietary, nationally supported medical gas equipment. Leadership emphasizes an "old fashion" commitment to customer service, backed by a team with deep backgrounds in sales, marketing, manufacturing, and engineering. When standard products do not fit, the company evaluates the application and develops special packages tailored to the facility''s needs.', certifications=ARRAY['NFPA 99','UL 508A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical air system design and assembly", "Medical vacuum system design and assembly", "Pipeline product distribution (manifolds, outlets, zone valves, alarms)", "Laboratory air system design", "Custom medical gas package engineering", "Installation and field service", "NFPA 99 compliance consulting", "UL 508A control panel fabrication"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Medical Devices", "Laboratory", "University Research", "Hospital"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Hitachi oil-less reciprocating scroll compressors", "Busch multi-claw vacuum pumps"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Medical air systems using Hitachi oil-less scroll compressors", "Medical vacuum systems with Busch multi-claw technology", "Pipeline products sourced through technology partnerships", "Custom engineering for non-standard medical gas applications", "Nationwide installation and service of own equipment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Charlotte, North Carolina -> db", "Pattons Inc. began selling medical air packages in 1980 -> /", "Patton''s Medical created in 2008 to sell and service own equipment -> /", "ELGi USA purchased Pattons Inc. and Patton''s Medical in 2012 -> /", "Medical air systems use Hitachi oil-less scroll compressors -> /", "Medical vacuum systems use Busch multi-claw technology -> /", "Pipeline products include universal medical manifolds, outlets, zone valves, alarms -> /", "Products meet or exceed NFPA 99; control panels UL 508A approved -> /", "Custom package engineering for specific applications -> /", "Serves hospitals, labs, universities -> /", "Commitment to customer service with experienced team -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Deciding to sell and service our own medical gas equipment nationwide, we created Pattons Medical in 2008.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='patton-s-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Paul Downs Cabinetmakers operates from Bridgeport, Pennsylvania, where it designs and builds custom conference tables and hand‑crafted furniture.

The shop produces a wide range of conference tables—large boardroom tables, U‑ and V‑shaped configurations, modular and reconfigurable systems, and tables engineered for videoconferencing with integrated A/V equipment. The workflow moves from real‑time virtual design collaboration through fabrication, finishing, assembly, and inspection, with the company reporting that it builds hundreds of modular tables each year. All pieces are assembled and inspected before shipping across North America.

Customers include federal agencies purchasing through GSA contracts, corporate offices, architects, interior designers, and furniture dealers who need tailored solutions for secure facilities, hard‑to‑fit rooms, or branding‑intensive spaces. The firm also works directly with end users seeking logo inlays in wood, laminate, metal, or vinyl.

Paul Downs emphasizes a blend of advanced engineering and traditional craftsmanship, offering real‑time design revisions via video call, upgradeable technology integration, and a willingness to execute designs that other manufacturers decline. The company positions itself as a problem‑solver for unique conference‑room challenges.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom conference table design and engineering", "Fabrication and finishing", "Assembly and inspection", "A/V integration and wiring management", "Logo inlay (wood, laminate, metal, vinyl, carving, engraving)", "Modular and reconfigurable table manufacturing", "Videoconferencing table integration", "Project management", "Shipping and installation", "Secure facility table fabrication", "Hard-to-fit room solutions"], "industries": ["Government (GSA)", "Corporate offices", "Architecture and interior design firms", "Furniture dealers", "Videoconferencing facilities", "Secure government facilities"], "materials": ["Wood", "Laminate", "Metal", "Vinyl"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Hundreds of modular and reconfigurable custom conference tables per year", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Real-time virtual design collaboration with live revisions", "Integrated A/V technology with upgradeable wiring", "Hundreds of modular and reconfigurable tables produced annually", "Custom logo inlays in wood, laminate, metal, and vinyl", "North American shipping and installation"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bridgeport, Pennsylvania -> db", "Company name: Paul Downs Cabinetmakers -> db", "Description: builds custom conference tables and hand-crafted furniture -> db", "Website: custom-conference-tables.com -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db", "Produces custom conference tables, modular, reconfigurable, videoconferencing, logo inlays -> /", "Process: design/engineering, fabrication/finishing, assembly/inspection, delivery/installation -> /", "Volume: hundreds of modular tables per year -> /", "Industries: Government/GSA, corporate, architects, interior designers, furniture dealers -> /", "Materials: wood, laminate, metal, vinyl for inlays -> /", "Differentiators: real-time design changes, integrated A/V, upgradeable wiring, unique solutions -> /", "Ships throughout North America -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We build beautiful, durable, and practical custom conference room tables and other hand-crafted furniture", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/paul-downs-cabinetmakers/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paul-downs-cabinetmakers' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Paul Renwick Textiles operates from New York, New York, where Scottish designer Paul Renwick established the studio after a career spanning fashion ateliers and interior projects. Renwick spent decades creating patterns and products for fashion houses, developing a distinctive command of scale, rhythm, and ornament that now defines the brand''s hand-embroidered textiles.

The company produces hand-embroidered textiles through a dedicated partnership with a workroom in Nepal, where each piece is meticulously crafted using vegetable-dyed threads on organic linen and cotton. The process emphasizes patient, deliberate artistry, with Renwick overseeing production to ensure integrity in every stitch. The collection spans designs suitable for both sleek urban apartments and storied country houses.

Renwick founded the venture on a lifelong passion for the decorative arts and a commitment to personal expression rather than trend-chasing. The differentiator lies in the fusion of historical reference with contemporary sensibility, executed through a transparent, human-scale supply chain that prioritizes material integrity and artisanal patience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand embroidery", "Textile design", "Pattern development", "Vegetable dyeing", "Organic material sourcing", "Artisanal oversight"], "industries": ["Luxury interior design", "Fashion", "Home textiles", "Decorative arts", "Residential interiors", "Contract interiors"], "materials": ["Vegetable-dyed threads", "Organic linen", "Organic cotton"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-embroidered production overseen via Nepalese workroom partnership", "Vegetable-dyed threads on organic linen and cotton", "Designs sourced from historical archives with modern intuition", "Personal expression prioritized over trend cycles", "Patient, deliberate artistry as a core value"], "facts_used": ["Scottish designer Paul Renwick with decades of experience -> /about", "Career bridging fashion ateliers and interior projects -> /about", "Created patterns and products for leading fashion houses -> /about", "Partnership with workroom in Nepal for handcrafting -> /about", "Uses vegetable-dyed threads, organic linen and cotton -> /about", "Hand-embroidered textiles -> /about", "Headquartered in New York, New York -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "meticulous handcrafting of each piece", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paul-renwick-textiles' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Payoff Solar is based in South Jordan, Utah, and was founded in 2024 by Matt Newman, who serves as chief executive, along with partners JD McBride and Kip Denning. The company began as a small team of renewable-energy advocates aiming to make solar power accessible, affordable, and hassle-free for homeowners and businesses.

The firm operates as a full-service solar provider, supplying high-efficiency photovoltaic panels and advanced battery storage systems while also handling consultation, system design, permitting, installation, and ongoing maintenance. It offers both stationary and mobile system configurations and allows customers to perform portions of the installation themselves to reduce costs. Pricing is advertised at $1.50 per watt, significantly below the typical $3–4 per watt charged by many installers.

Payoff Solar serves residential and commercial customers seeking to reduce energy expenses and carbon emissions. Its process moves from a preliminary property assessment to a detailed proposal with projected savings, followed by professional installation and final inspection. The company states it has helped thousands of clients lower their utility bills and shrink their environmental footprint.

The business distinguishes itself by targeting a financial payback period of three to four years, far shorter than the industry norm of 15 to 20 years. Its stated values of innovation, sustainability, and affordability guide a model that combines equipment supply with turnkey service, aiming to make renewable energy a practical investment for a broader audience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Consultation", "System design", "Site assessment", "Proposal generation", "Permitting", "Installation", "Final inspection", "Ongoing maintenance", "Solar panel supply", "Energy storage supply", "Stationary system configuration", "Mobile system configuration"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Solar energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Financial payback target of 3\u20134 years versus industry average of 15\u201320", "Equipment pricing at $1.50 per watt", "Option for customer self-installation to lower total cost", "Full-service scope from site assessment through maintenance", "High-efficiency panels and battery storage offered"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2024 -> /about", "Headquarters South Jordan, Utah -> db", "Founder Matt Newman (CEO) -> /about", "Partners JD McBride and Kip Denning -> /about", "Mission: make solar accessible, affordable, hassle-free -> /", "Full-service provider: consultation, design, installation, maintenance -> /about", "Products: high-efficiency solar panels, advanced battery storage -> /", "Pricing $1.50 per watt -> /", "Option for customer self-installation -> /", "Target payback 3-4 years vs industry 15-20 -> /", "Values: Innovation, Sustainability, Affordability -> /about", "Helped thousands of customers -> /about", "Process: assess, proposal, install -> /", "System types: Stationary, Mobile -> /", "Serves homeowners and businesses -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "full-