UPDATE companies SET description='Peak Automation & Electrical, LLC is based in Dickinson, North Dakota. The company operates as a limited liability company providing automation and electrical services to industrial clients across the state. While the founding year and ownership structure beyond the LLC designation are not publicly disclosed, the firm has built a reputation serving the region''s energy and processing sectors.

The company delivers a range of services including electrical construction with a North Dakota Master Electrician on record, 24/7/365 electrical service, SCADA development on the Inductive Automation Ignition platform, flow meter setup and calibration for orifice, magnetic, turbine, mass, and Coriolis meters, as well as LACT unit commissioning. It also installs and maintains wired, wireless, and radio network instrumentation such as guided wave radars, ultrasonic level sensors, and pressure transmitters. Programming and troubleshooting cover PLC, DCS, and HMI systems from Allen-Bradley, IDEC, GE, Scadapack, and multiple HMI brands. Engineering services encompass automation consulting, corporate standards development, program management, panel design, FAT/SAT testing, and project documentation using AutoCAD Electrical.

Peak serves industries including cryogenic processing, power generation, salt water disposal, oil and gas production sites, tank batteries, compressor stations, offshore platforms, chemical processing plants, and food and beverage manufacturing facilities.

The company emphasizes a safety-first culture, holding memberships in ISNetworld and PEC, and highlights a management team with over 75 years of combined automation and electrical experience. Its differentiators include round-the-clock service availability, Ignition platform certification, and a focus on developing corporate automation standards for clients.', certifications=ARRAY['Inductive Automation Ignition Platform Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical construction", "24/7/365 electrical service", "SCADA development (Ignition platform)", "Flow meter setup, calibration, and maintenance", "LACT unit setup, commissioning, and maintenance", "Wired, wireless, and radio network instrumentation installation and maintenance", "PLC, DCS, and HMI custom programming and troubleshooting", "Engineering services", "Automation consulting", "Corporate automation standards development", "Program management", "Standard AOI block development", "MOC (Management of Change) processes", "Panel design and I/O layout", "FAT and SAT testing and commissioning", "Project documentation (AutoCAD Electrical, cause & effect matrix, control narrative, I/O list)"], "industries": ["Cryogenic processing", "Power generation", "Salt water disposal", "Oil and gas production", "Tank batteries", "Compressor stations", "Offshore platforms", "Chemical processing", "Food and beverage manufacturing", "Drilling solutions"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Allen-Bradley PLCs", "IDEC PLCs", "GE PLCs", "Scadapack RTUs", "Red Lion HMI", "Proface HMI", "PanelView HMI", "Magelis HMI", "Maple HMI", "Totalflow", "Emerson ROC 800", "Emerson FloBoss 107", "Inductive Automation Ignition SCADA platform", "Cygnet SCADA", "FactoryTalk", "Wonderware", "iCONICS"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7/365 electrical service response", "Inductive Automation Ignition Platform certified", "ISNetworld and PEC safety program memberships", "Management team with 75+ years combined experience", "North Dakota Master Electrician on record for construction"], "facts_used": ["Location: Dickinson, ND -> /", "Company type: professional services (automation, instrumentation, controls, SCADA) -> /", "Management team combined 75+ years experience -> /", "Safety memberships: ISNetworld, PEC -> /", "Electrical construction with ND Master on Record -> /", "24/7/365 electrical service -> /", "SCADA development: Ignition Platform Certified -> /", "Flow meter setup/calibration: orifice, mag, turbine, mass, Coriolis, LACT -> /", "Instrumentation installs: guided wave radar, float, ultrasonic, pressure transmitters, level switches, tuning forks, pressure switches -> /", "PLC/DCS/HMI programming: Allen-Bradley, IDEC, GE, Scadapack, multiple HMI brands -> /", "Engineering services: consulting, standards, program management, AOI blocks, MOC, panel design, FAT/SAT, documentation -> /", "Industries served: cryogenic, power gen, SWD, oil/gas production, tank batteries, compressor stations, offshore, chemical, food/beverage -> /", "Customer type: industry leaders, drilling solutions companies -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Peak Automation & Electrical, LLC provides professional services to industry leaders across North Dakota. We are dedicated to providing leading-edge Automation, Instrumentation, Controls, Programming, Measurement, and Scada Development.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='peak-automation-and-electrical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Peerless Electronic Supplies traces its roots to 1932 when C.C. Baines founded the Peerless Electronic Equipment Company in Louisville, Kentucky. The business has continued across three generations and remains headquartered in Louisville, operating from a 25,000-square-foot facility on one acre.

Today the company operates as a broad-line business-to-business distributor of electronic components and assemblies. It stocks products from more than 100 manufacturers, including over 40 franchised lines such as Belden, Fluke, Omron, Panduit, and TE Connectivity. In addition to distribution, Peerless provides value-added services including custom cable assemblies, custom-length DIN rail, terminal block assemblies, bar coding, kitting, labeling, and special packaging.

The customer base spans OEM, MRO, institutional, and contractor sectors, with industrial sales split roughly 80 percent OEM and 20 percent MRO. A field sales team covers Kentucky, Indiana, Michigan, Illinois, Ohio, and Wisconsin, supporting regional accounts with local inventory and a $5 minimum order.

Peerless states its mission is to deliver quality products on time at competitive prices with the highest level of service. The company emphasizes its combined staff experience of over 200 years in the electronics industry and a quality policy focused on providing products that conform to customer requirements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bar Coding", "Custom Cable Assemblies", "Custom Length DIN Rail", "Custom Terminal Block Assemblies", "Dedicated Inventory", "Kitting, Labeling & Packaging", "Special Packaging & Marking"], "industries": ["OEM", "MRO", "Institutional", "Contractor"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low $5 minimum order", "Local inventory in 25,000 sq ft facility", "Over 100 manufacturers and 40 franchised lines stocked", "Buying group partnership for additional franchised lines", "Over 200 years combined sales experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1932 by C.C. Baines -> /about", "Three generations of operation -> /about", "Headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky -> /about, db", "25,000 sq ft facility on one acre -> /about", "Broad-line B2B distributor of electronic components and assemblies -> /about", "Represents over 100 manufacturers and 40 franchised lines -> /about", "Value-added services: custom cable assemblies, custom-length DIN rail, terminal block assemblies, bar coding, kitting, labeling, special packaging -> /about", "Customer base: OEM, MRO, institutional, contractor sectors -> /about", "Industrial sales split 80% OEM, 20% MRO -> /about", "Field sales coverage across KY, IN, MI, IL, OH, WI -> /about", "$5 minimum order -> /about", "Mission: quality products on time at competitive prices with highest service -> /about", "Combined staff experience over 200 years -> /about", "Quality policy: products conforming to customer requirements -> /about", "Product categories listed on homepage -> /", "Contact address: 1815 South 7th Street, Louisville, KY 40208 -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "operating as Peerless Electronic Supplies, we continue to be a broad line business-to-business distributor of electronic components and assemblies", "founded_year": "1932", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "$5.00", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='peerless-electronic-supplies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pelican Wire operates from Naples, Florida, as a custom wire manufacturer specializing in engineered resistance and heating wire solutions. The company does not publish a founding date or founder names in its public materials, and ownership details are not disclosed.

The shop focuses on custom-engineered wire rather than catalog products, producing high-flex life wire for robotic motion control, heating wire for fluid transfer systems, fine-gauge wire (40–45 AWG) for aerospace sensors, high-temperature wire for autoclaves, ultra-fine wire for e-textiles, and cryogenic-grade wire. It also designs resistance heating wire for composite tooling such as wind turbine blade molds. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are provided.

Pelican Wire serves wind energy, aerospace and aviation, robotics, radiant flooring (RV, residential, and commercial), automotive (heated seats, fluid transfer, emissions systems), autoclave, UAV, cryogenics, medical devices, and e-textiles. The company notes partnerships with numerous medical device manufacturers and supplies wire for aerospace robotics, automotive sensors, and wearable technology.

The company states it differentiates itself by rejecting pre-made solutions: it operates with no standard print, offering fully custom wire designs. It also runs an ON-DEMAND program for immediate shipment of stocked premium wire and provides a Product Design Tool Kit with size charts, insulation guides, and calculators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom resistance wire design", "High-flex life wire manufacturing", "Heating wire for fluid transfer systems", "Fine gauge wire drawing (40\u201345 AWG)", "High-temperature wire for autoclaves", "Ultra-fine wire for e-textiles", "Cryogenic wire solutions", "Composite tooling heating wire (wind turbine blade molds)", "Aerospace sensor wire", "Automotive sensor wire", "Medical device heated wire", "Radiant floor heating wire", "ON-DEMAND stocked wire program"], "industries": ["Wind Energy", "Aerospace & Aviation", "Robotics", "Radiant Flooring", "Automotive", "Autoclave", "UAV", "Cryogenics", "Medical Devices", "E-Textiles", "Composite Manufacturing", "Wearable Technology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Immediate shipment for ON-DEMAND stocked wire", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No standard print \u2013 fully custom wire solutions", "ON-DEMAND premium wire for immediate shipment", "Product Design Tool Kit with size charts, insulation types, calculators", "Specialized in high-flex life wire for robotic motion control", "Expertise in fine gauge wire (40\u201345 AWG) for aerospace sensors"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Naples, Florida -> db", "Description: Wind Turbine Blade Mold Heating: Resistance Wire Design for Composite Manufacturing -> db", "Custom wire shop with no standard print -> /", "Industries served list (Wind Energy, Aerospace & Aviation, Robotics, Radiant Flooring, Automotive, Autoclave, UAV, Cryogenics, Medical Devices, E-Textiles) -> /", "ON-DEMAND: Premium Wire Available for Immediate Shipment -> /", "Product Design Tool Kit with size charts, wire insulation types, calculators -> /", "High-flex life wire for robotic motion control -> /", "Heating wire for heated fluid transfer systems -> /", "Fine gauge wire for aerospace sensors (40\u201345 AWG) -> /", "Partnered with numerous medical device manufacturers -> /", "Resistance wire solutions for wind turbine blade mold heating -> /", "High-precision resistance wire for aerospace robotics & motion control -> /", "Powering the future of wearable technology: e-textile innovation -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Wire Solutions Manufacturer USA", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pelican-wire' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Penn Metal Fabricators Inc. was founded in 1969 in Ebensburg, Pennsylvania. The company operates a 175,000-square-foot facility there, housing complete fabrication and machine shops under one roof.

The shop performs all operations from raw material to finished part, working from customer drawings or CAD files. Capabilities include CNC laser cutting of sheet and tube, plasma cutting, punching, bending, automatic sawing, and tube bending; CNC vertical machining, horizontal milling and boring, and lathe turning; robotic and manual MIG/TIG welding; and finishing via powder coat, wet enamel, CARC, and chemical conversion coating. The company also handles assembly and packaging, and maintains an in-house repair shop to keep equipment running.

Customers span the U.S. Military, which has sourced troop-support equipment and spare parts for more than 40 years; the U.S. Postal Service, which buys bulk-mail handling equipment and sorting-room furniture; the construction sector, receiving scissor- and boom-lift components; and the railroad industry, where parts are welded into rail cars. The about-us page adds aviation, biomedical, and electrical markets to the list.

Penn Metal emphasizes its ability to deliver both one-off prototypes and long production runs on schedule, backed by an ISO 9001:2000 quality system and FaroArm CMM inspection. The firm says its combined staff experience exceeds 160 years and that its processes meet the strict requirements of both the military and the postal service.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC Laser Cutting (sheet/plate)", "CNC Tubing Laser Cutting", "CNC Plasma Cutting", "CNC Punching", "CNC Bending", "Automatic Sawing", "CNC Tube Bending", "CNC Vertical Machining", "CNC Horizontal Milling / Boring", "CNC Lathe Turning / Boring", "Drilling & Tapping", "Robotic Welding", "Manual MIG Welding", "Manual TIG Welding", "Powder Coating", "Wet Coating", "CARC Coating", "Bare Metal Finishing", "Chemical Conversion Coating (aluminum)", "Assembly", "Packaging", "Quality Inspection (FaroArm CMM)", "Deep Draw"], "industries": ["U.S. Military", "U.S. Postal Service", "Construction", "Railroad", "Aviation", "Biomedical", "Electrical"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["FaroArm CMM"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete in-house fabrication from raw material to finished product", "175,000 sq. ft. facility with dedicated equipment repair shop", "ISO 9001:2000 quality system with FaroArm CMM inspection", "Over 40 years supplying the U.S. Military", "Serves U.S. Postal Service, construction, railroad, aviation, biomedical, and electrical markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1969 -> /about-us", "175,000 sq. ft. plant in Ebensburg, PA -> /about-us", "Supplies U.S. Military for over 40 years -> /", "Supplies U.S. Postal Service with bulk mail handling equipment -> /", "Produces scissor and boom lift parts for construction -> /", "Manufactures parts welded into rail cars -> /", "Industries: Aviation, Biomedical, Electrical -> /about-us", "Capabilities: CNC laser cutting, tubing laser cutting, plasma cutting, punching, bending, sawing, tube bending, vertical machining, horizontal milling/boring, lathe turning/boring, drilling & tapping, robotic welding, manual MIG/TIG welding, powder coating, wet coating, CARC coating, bare metal finishing, assembly, packaging -> / and /capabilities", "ISO9001:2000 Quality System -> /", "FaroArm CMM inspection -> /", "In-house repair shop -> /about-us", "Complete fabrication from raw material to finished product -> / and /about-us", "Over 160 years combined experience -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "In our 175,000 sq. ft. plant in Ebensburg, PA Penn Metal Fabricators offer complete metal fabrication from raw materials to finished products from customers'' drawings and or CAD CAM files.", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='penn-metal-fabricators-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Penny Fab, LLC operates from Columbus, Ohio, where it provides custom metal design and fabrication services. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, nor are its founders named in available materials. The business presents itself as a precision metal fabrication shop.

The shop offers a range of metalworking processes including design engineering, laser cutting, punching, forming, machining, and welding. A 4,000-watt laser cuts sheet metal up to one inch thick, and a recently added three-axis mill expands precision machining capacity. The company describes its capabilities as expert design, precision fabrication, and rapid turnaround at competitive prices. Facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not specified.

The company does not list specific industries or customer types in its public materials. Its services target any client requiring custom sheet-metal parts and fabricated assemblies, with design engineering support to move concepts into production.

