UPDATE companies SET description='Perry''s Metal Fabrication operates from Mooresville, North Carolina, in the heart of the Lake Norman region. It remains a family-owned operation, with Perry serving as both owner and lead fabricator.

It works with aluminum, steel, stainless steel, 4130 chromoly, titanium, and sheet metal. Capabilities range from one-off brackets and frames to larger-scale production runs, including architectural metalwork such as gates, railings, and furniture frames, as well as repair and reinforcement of existing parts. The facility houses lathes, mills, and press brakes for cutting, shaping, and forming.

Customers include homeowners, small businesses, auto and marine enthusiasts, and industrial clients across the Mooresville and Lake Norman area. Concrete projects include a custom roll cage for an exotic auto shop, sprint car chassis modifications, a fabricated race hauler, a funnel and parts for a local ice cream shop, and a fabrication project for a national warehouse chain. The shop also serves motorsports teams with specialized race car fabrication.

