UPDATE companies SET description='Phoenix Solar Panel Systems operates from Phoenix, Arizona, serving the metropolitan area and surrounding communities. The company was founded by Steven Smith, J.D., known as "Solar Steve Esquire," after he worked at several Valley solar companies and observed what he describes as an extreme lack of professionalism, honesty, and customer service in the industry. Smith started the business to provide a transparent alternative in a market he characterizes as having zero regulation and high turnover.

The firm does not perform installations itself. Instead, it helps homeowners and businesses explore solar options — grid-tied, off-grid, and battery-backup systems — and connects them with independent installers. Customers contract directly with the installer performing the work. The company also coordinates related services such as home energy audits, attic insulation, duct sealing, EV charger installation, solar water heaters, solar panel cleaning, bird proofing, removal and reinstallation, and solar carport or patio cover projects. It provides educational resources including an Arizona Solar FAQ, cost guides, and a list of questions to ask solar companies.

The primary customers are residential property owners in the Phoenix area and commercial property owners seeking to reduce energy costs. The company references work with Arizona Public Service (APS) and Salt River Project (SRP) utility territories. Commercial clients include businesses looking to cut operating expenses and meet clean-energy goals. The service also supports off-grid properties requiring custom battery and backup designs.

Smith states the company was created to bring honesty, integrity, and transparency to the solar industry. The model emphasizes educating customers rather than selling, presenting both positives and negatives of solar ownership, and building long-term relationships over short-term commissions. The founder describes the business as being in the "people business, not the solar business," with a goal of cleaning up the residential solar market through fair, informed decision-making.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar consulting and education", "Independent installer referral and connection", "Residential grid-tied solar system design assistance", "Commercial solar system design assistance", "Off-grid solar system design assistance", "Solar battery and storage consultation", "Home energy audits", "Solar panel cleaning and maintenance coordination", "Solar panel bird proofing coordination", "Solar panel removal and reinstallation coordination", "Solar carport and patio cover design assistance", "EV charger installation coordination", "Attic insulation and duct sealing coordination", "Solar water heater consultation"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Energy efficiency", "Solar energy storage", "Home energy auditing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customers contract directly with the independent installer", "Educating-not-selling consultation model", "Present all positives and negatives of solar ownership", "Free quote calls and educational resource library", "Focus on long-term customer relationships over short-term commissions"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location -> db", "Founder Steven Smith, J.D. -> /about-us", "Founder background working at Valley solar companies -> /about-us", "Mission: honesty, integrity, transparency -> /about-us", "Business model: connect customers with independent installers -> /", "Customers contract directly with installer -> /", "Services: residential, commercial, off-grid, battery backup, energy audits -> /, /services", "Utility references: APS and SRP -> /", "Educational resources: FAQ, cost guides, questions to ask -> /", "Related services: insulation, duct sealing, EV charger, water heaters, cleaning, bird proofing, removal/reinstall, carports -> /services", "Target customers: homeowners and businesses in Phoenix metro -> /, /services", "No manufacturing, no certifications, no equipment listed -> all pages"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Phoenix Solar Panel Systems helps homeowners in Phoenix and the surrounding Phoenix metropolitan area explore solar options and connect with independent installers. Customers contract directly with the independent installer performing the work.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='phoenix-solar-panel-systems-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Photonworks Engineering is based in Honolulu, Hawaii, and was founded in 2003 by Tim Johnsson. Johnsson, a recipient of the ABC 2010 Excellence in Construction Award for multi-family developments, established the company to connect people with cheaper and cleaner sources of power while preserving Hawaii’s natural beauty.

The company provides end-to-end energy solutions: solar photovoltaic design and installation, battery energy storage systems, microgrid engineering, full-service electrical construction, energy efficiency retrofits, PV system monitoring and maintenance, and eco-friendly development. Photonworks handles site assessment, engineering, permitting, construction, commissioning, and long-term operations and maintenance, offering up to two years of no-charge O&M after installation. It also structures power purchase agreements with zero capital expense and zero-down financing. The firm reports serving thousands of customers across Hawaii and beyond, with a project portfolio that includes commercial, institutional, and government sites.

Photonworks serves residential homeowners, commercial property owners, educational institutions, non-profits, and government agencies. Named projects include Hanalani Schools, Boys and Girls Club of Hawaii, Joint Base Pearl Harbor, Aiea Public Library, Kailua Waste Water Facility, Kahauiki Village, Hawaii Pacific University, Century West, USSF Space Fence, and the Board of Water Supply. The company works closely with Hawaiian Electric (HECO) on interconnection agreements and grid services.

The mission is to exceed expectations through one-stop engineering-to-construction solutions, straightforward technical staff rather than salespeople, and a focus on energy autonomy and resilience for Hawaii’s transition to 100% renewable energy.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design and installation", "Battery energy storage system design and installation", "Microgrid engineering and grid services", "Full-service electrical construction", "Energy efficiency audits and retrofits", "PV system monitoring and maintenance", "Site assessment and shading analysis", "Permitting and interconnection management", "Commissioning and project closeout", "Operations and maintenance (O&M) services", "Power purchase agreement (PPA) structuring", "Eco-friendly development consulting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Government / military", "Education", "Non-profit", "Utility / grid services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One-stop full engineering to construction solutions", "Up to two years free operations and maintenance after installation", "Zero-down financing and power purchase agreements with zero capital expense", "Local Hawaii team dedicated to 100% renewable energy goals", "Straightforward technical staff, not salespeople"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 by Tim Johnsson -> /about", "Tim Johnsson founder, ABC 2010 Excellence in Construction Award -> /about", "Paul Orem CEO, licensed journeyman electrician, 25 years experience -> /about", "Randall Bricker COO, 28 years experience -> /about", "Serving Hawaii over 18 years -> /about", "Services: Solar PV, Battery Storage, Microgrids, Full Electrical Construction, Energy Efficiency, Monitoring, Eco-Friendly Development, PPAs -> / and /services", "Zero down financing, PPAs with zero capital expense -> /", "Up to 2 years free O&M after installation -> /services", "Projects: Hanalani Schools, Boys and Girls Club, Joint Base Pearl Harbor, Aiea Public Library, Kailua Waste Water Facility, Kahauiki Village, Hawaii Pacific University, Century West, USSF Space Fence, Board of Water Supply -> /about", "Thousands of customers in Hawaii and beyond -> /", "14 years experience with solar PV systems -> /services", "Work with HECO on interconnection -> /services", "Mission: highest quality, best customer experience, clients become fans -> /", "Most residential clients referrals, commercial repeat customers -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "PhotonWorks Engineering is a Hawaii-based construction and energy solutions company... Design Build Renewable Energy Contractor... Full Service Electrical Construction", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='photonworks-engineering' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company serves Marion County and surrounding areas from a 78,000-square-foot indoor warehouse that stores more than 65,000 cataloged parts.

The operation disassembles late-model vehicles piece by piece, then cleans, inspects, and tests each component before entering it into a computerized inventory system. Parts range from engines, transmissions, and axles to doors, bumpers, windshields, and lighting assemblies. All inventory is housed indoors to protect against weather, and fluids such as freon, coolant, oil, gasoline, and brake fluid are recovered and recycled in accordance with environmental standards.

Free regional delivery is offered, and customers can search the inventory online or visit the warehouse for in-person assistance.

