UPDATE companies SET description='The Londonderry, New Hampshire branch of Piedmont Plastics traces its roots to Plastic Supply, Inc., a local plastics distributor that served the region for more than 47 years. On September 12, 2019, Piedmont Plastics acquired PSI and integrated the operation into its North American network of branch locations. The facility is managed by Jaime Lemos.

The branch operates as both a stocking distributor and a fabrication shop. In-house fabrication capabilities span CNC routing and laser cutting, milling, drilling, turning, welding, bonding, edging, buffing, sanding, sandblasting, and thermoforming. The shop runs four Mori Seiki CNC vertical milling centers, a Mori Seiki AL2 CNC lathe, a Saeilo Sprint 20 CNC lathe, a Hardinge DSM59 lathe, four Bridgeport CNC vertical mills, a HAAS TM2P vertical milling center, a Drypoll vacuum thermoforming machine, a Gruenberg anneal oven, and an Accu Finish diamond grinder. Assembly services include mechanical fastening, welding, custom wiring harness assembly, bonding, riveting, and packing.

The location serves customers throughout southern and central New Hampshire, with listed service areas covering Manchester, Derry, Nashua, Salem, Merrimack, Hudson, and dozens of surrounding communities. While the company does not specify target industries in its public materials, the material range and fabrication services suggest it supports manufacturers, prototypers, and maintenance operations requiring plastic components.

