UPDATE companies SET description='Pittsburgh Plastics Manufacturing was founded in 1977 by Jim Zona in Butler, Pennsylvania, just north of Pittsburgh. A Penn State graduate, Zona began by developing gel insoles—essentially "waterbeds for your feet"—and built the company into a women-owned custom manufacturer of gel and foam cushioning solutions.

Operating from a 91,000-square-foot facility with 50–75 employees, the company formulates more than 35 proprietary polymer blends—including IsoGel®, IsoFoam®, and GELoam®—and handles mold design, CNC machining, prototyping, and full-scale production in-house. An internal polymer scientist and CAD designer support rapid turnaround, while lean practices such as KAIZEN and 5S drive efficiency.

PPM serves medical and healthcare, safety, industrial, hot-and-cold therapy, and foot-care markets, supplying OEMs and private-label brands across the United States, Europe, and Canada. The facility is FDA registered, ISO 13485:2016 certified, and QRS-compliant with process validations for medical components, adhering to CGMP and TQMS standards.

The company emphasizes its U.S.-based, women-owned status and a "PPM Promise" of 100 percent precision, accuracy, and on-time delivery. Complete manufacturing traceability, pre-certified raw materials, and quality checks at every stage reinforce its differentiation in custom cushioning.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA registered','QRS-compliant','CGMP','TQMS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom gel and foam cushioning manufacturing", "Proprietary polymer formulation (IsoGel\u00ae, IsoFoam\u00ae, GELoam\u00ae)", "In-house mold design and CNC machining", "Rapid prototyping", "Production scaling", "Finishing services", "In-house R&D with polymer scientist and CAD designer", "Lean manufacturing (KAIZEN, 5S)", "Quality control per ISO standards", "Private label product development", "OEM contract manufacturing", "Medical component process validation", "Raw material inspection and traceability", "Dual-durometer gel production", "Silicone gel manufacturing", "Hydrogel manufacturing", "Polyurethane foam manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical and healthcare", "Safety equipment", "Industrial", "Hot and cold therapy", "Foot care"], "materials": ["Super-soft gels (Shore 000 durometer)", "Dual-durometer gels", "Silicone gels", "Hydrogels", "Polyurethane foams", "Proprietary polymers (IsoGel\u00ae, IsoFoam\u00ae, GELoam\u00ae)"], "equipment": ["CNC machine for mold making"], "volume": "Small to large scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary polymer library with 35+ custom formulations (IsoGel\u00ae, IsoFoam\u00ae, GELoam\u00ae)", "In-house polymer scientist, CAD designer, and CNC machining for rapid mold-to-part turnaround", "Women-owned and operated U.S. manufacturer with full traceability", "ISO 13485:2016 certified, FDA registered, and QRS-compliant for medical components", "Lean manufacturing culture (KAIZEN, 5S) driving efficiency and quality"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 by Jim Zona -> /about", "Women-owned cu