UPDATE companies SET description='Plastics Unlimited operates from a 130,000-square-foot facility in Preston, Iowa. The company was founded in 1993 by Terry, Nancy, and Gene Kieffer on their family farm after the physical toll of livestock farming prompted them to seek a less labor-intensive venture. They purchased a used thermoforming machine at auction, installed it in a machine shed, and began producing dunnage for local agricultural customers.

Today the manufacturer provides custom thermoforming (both heavy- and thin-gauge), composites — including its proprietary Tooless Engineered Composites (TEC)® process — and urethane molding. In-house design and tooling teams work alongside CNC robotic trimming and secondary assembly operations. The facility has grown from a 15,000-square-foot industrial park building acquired in 1997 to its current footprint, supporting high-volume production for a range of industries.

The company serves agriculture, construction, dunnage, material handling, medical, OEM, outdoor/recreation, aerospace, industrial, and transportation markets.

