UPDATE companies SET description='Plexus Corporation is headquartered in Nampa, Idaho. The company traces its roots to an integrated group of people working together to solve complex challenges, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The company provides end-to-end product realization services spanning design, manufacturing, and aftermarket support. Its capabilities include product design and development, new product introduction, contract manufacturing, supply chain management, sustaining services, and failure analysis at the board, sub-assembly, and system levels. Plexus operates a global footprint across four continents, with manufacturing sites positioned near customer end markets, though specific facility sizes and headcount figures are not disclosed.

Plexus serves highly regulated sectors including aerospace and defense, healthcare and life sciences, industrial, and semiconductor capital equipment. A documented case study highlights a partnership with a global construction and mining equipment manufacturer, where Plexus addressed circuit board failures in power inverters for hybrid wheel loaders, bulldozers, and underground electric mining vehicles. Another customer, Bevi, relies on Plexus to manufacture smart water dispensers in Appleton, Wisconsin.

Plexus emphasizes a culture built on five values: growing people, building belonging, innovating responsibly, delivering excellence, and creating customer success. The company cites nearly 50 years of experience designing and building printed circuit boards as a foundation for its engineering depth, and it differentiates through integrated engineering, manufacturing, and supply chain solutions delivered through a single point of contact across its global network.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Design & Development", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Contract Manufacturing", "Supply Chain Solutions", "Sustaining Services", "Failure Analysis (board, sub-assembly, system level)", "PCB Design and Assembly", "Grid Automation Services: Complex High-Level Assembly", "Turnkey Product Development", "Design for Excellence (DFX)", "PCB Rework Services", "Life Cycle Assessments", "Test Strategies and Solutions", "Product Strategy & Requirements Management", "Manufacturing Process Optimization", "Quick-turnaround Design Services", "Custom Power Supply Integration", "Supplier Evaluation and Selection", "Global Manufacturing Footprint Management"], "industries": ["Aerospace / Defense", "Healthcare / Life Sciences", "Industrial", "Semiconductor Capital Equipment", "Heavy Equipment (Construction and Mining)", "Industrial OEMs"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Failure Analysis Lab capable of board, sub-assembly, and system-level root cause analysis", "Nearly 50 years of experience designing and building thousands of PCBs", "Global footprint across four continents with centralized point of contact", "Class A paint finishing capabilities for harsh environments", "Integrated engineering, manufacturing, and supply chain solutions under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Nampa, Idaho -> db", "Global presence across four continents -> /about", "Serves Aerospace/Defense, Healt