UPDATE companies SET description='Popknot Wood operates from Rogers, Arkansas. The company was founded by John, a U.S. Army veteran, after he began teaching woodworking to his grandchildren in his home shop. What started as a family project building birdhouses, signs, and boxes evolved into a formal business when the family developed a marketing plan and launched a website. The venture is veteran-owned and family-driven.

The shop produces custom woodworking and restoration pieces using a mix of hand tools, power tools, CNC routing, and laser engraving. Its output includes furniture refurbishment, replacement parts for discontinued items, heirloom repairs, custom cutting boards (including state-shaped designs), wooden urns and memorial pieces, awards and presentation pieces, river tables, custom flags, and signs. All items are made in-house and shipped to all 50 states.

Customers range from individuals seeking personalized gifts or restored heirlooms to churches, ministries, and organizations needing faith-based creations, awards, or signage.

John credits his Army service for instilling discipline and integrity that guide every build. Faith informs the work as a form of stewardship, and the shop prioritizes local wood whenever possible. Popknot Wood was recognized as the Best Woodworker in Rogers, AR for 2026, reflecting its commitment to purpose-driven craftsmanship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Furniture restoration and repair", "Replacement part fabrication", "Heirloom restoration", "CNC routing", "Laser engraving and cutting", "Custom cutting board production", "Memorial and urn crafting", "Awards and presentation pieces", "River table construction", "Custom flag and sign making", "Faith-based woodworking"], "industries": ["Residential", "Religious institutions", "Memorial services", "Corporate awards and recognition", "Custom signage"], "materials": ["Local wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned and family-driven", "Sources local wood whenever possible", "Ships nationwide to all 50 states", "Faith-informed craftsmanship"], "facts_used": ["Operates from Rogers, Arkansas -> db", "Founded by John, a U.S. Army veteran -> /about", "Began as family project teaching grandchildren woodworking -> /about", "Developed business and marketing plan with family -> /about", "Veteran-owned and family-driven -> /about", "Produces custom woodworking and restoration using hand tools, power tools, CNC routing, laser engraving -> /", "Output includes furniture refurbishment, replacement parts, heirloom repairs, custom cutting boards, wooden urns, awards, river tables, custom flags, signs -> /", "Ships to all 50 states -> /about", "Serves residential clients, religious institutions, corporate buyers -> /about", "Army service instilled discipline and integrity -> /about", "Faith informs work as stewardship -> /about", "Prioritizes local wood -> /about", "Recognized as Best Woodworker in Rogers, AR (2026) -> /about", "Company type: Manufacturer -> inferred from description", "Ownership tags: Veteran-owned, Family-owned, Small business -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PopKnotWood specializes in custom woodworking, restoration, and precision-crafted pieces built with care and intention.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='popknot-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Porter Barn Wood operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where Thomas Porter founded the business in 2010 after years of woodworking experience. The company began when Porter and his friend Craig Suiter recognized a demand for quality reclaimed barn wood in the Phoenix area, initially unloading beams from Pennsylvania barns and opening a regular yard for public sales. Porter formed the LLC in 2012, and the venture has since grown into a family-owned operation with his wife Emy and their two children involved.

The company maintains a wood shop, metal shop, concrete shop, and finishing and contracting teams, allowing it to fabricate custom furniture, architectural accents, and structural elements from a wide range of materials. Services include milling, blacksmithing, CNC plasma cutting, CNC routing, laser engraving, and various finishing techniques such as lacquer, conversion varnish, and custom color matching. The shop also sources and sells reclaimed barn wood from Pennsylvania, Michigan, Ohio, Kentucky, Tennessee, and Iowa, as well as live-edge slabs salvaged from local forest-fire and beetle-kill sites.

Porter Barn Wood serves restaurants, hospitality venues, commercial contractors, luxury home builders, and residential remodelers. Projects have included dining tables for Surf City and Famé, a creative event space for The Duce, and whole-home remodels featuring custom cabinetry and built-ins. The facility has also hosted film crews for HGTV and PBS productions, taking advantage of its well-lit, climate-controlled workshops.

The company distinguishes itself by accepting customers'' own reclaimed materials — such as family barn wood or old warehouse metal — and integrating them into new builds. It also offers free woodworking and metalworking classes, rents its event tables, and emphasizes a collaborative approach with designers and architects to execute custom visions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metalworking", "Blacksmithing", "Woodworking", "Milling", "Furniture making", "Repairs", "Modifications", "Spindle duplication", "Production manufacturing", "CNC plasma cutting", "CNC routing", "Laser engraving", "Architectural photography", "Interior design photography", "Image licensing", "Finishing (lacquer, polyurethane, conversion varnish, waxes, oils)", "Custom finish matching", "3D CAD design", "Concept rendering", "Furniture design", "Reclaimed wood sourcing", "Live edge slab sourcing", "Custom fabrication", "Event space rental"], "industries": ["Restaurant", "Hospitality", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Interior design", "Film and television production", "Retail", "Event space"], "materials": ["Reclaimed barn wood", "Live edge slabs", "Wood", "Metal", "Glass", "Concrete", "Leather", "Plastic", "Styrofoam", "Acrylic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Accepts and incorporates customers'' own reclaimed materials into custom builds", "Offers free woodworking and metalworking classes and demonstrations", "Provides TV-friendly, climate-controlled shop space for film productions", "Collaborates directly with designers and architects to implement custom designs", "Supplies reclaimed barn wood from multiple states and locally salvaged live-edge slabs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 by Thomas Porter -> /about", "LLC formed in 2012 -> /about-us", "Family-owned, wife Emy and two children -> /about, /about-us", "Location: Phoenix, Arizona -> db, /about-us", "Wood shop, metal shop, concrete 