UPDATE companies SET description='Power Control Services is based in Broussard, Louisiana. The company traces its roots to 1996 when Walter Bergeron founded Synergy Technologies in a backyard workshop. The business was later renamed Power Control Services and has grown into a specialist in industrial electronic repair.

The shop focuses on repairing and rebuilding industrial electronics such as AC/DC drives, servo drives, industrial displays, power supplies, PLCs, and servomotors. Technicians work at ESD- and SMT-equipped rework stations using a proactive, component-level repair process backed by an extensive parts inventory and research system. The company advertises a standard five-day turnaround and says its pricing runs 35–50 percent below competitor rates.

Customers span power generation (Entergy), food processing (Tyson Foods, Coca-Cola), oil and gas (Parker Drilling, NOV, Transocean, Halliburton, Schlumberger), chemical manufacturing (Dow), and industrial distribution (ConocoPhillips, Disney World). The firm also partners with regional and national distributors to extend its reach.

Power Control Services says its differentiation comes from a ''Right Way, Right Away'' philosophy: certified technicians (IPC 7711/7721), generous warranties, innovative technology, and compliance with GSA and military ESD standards (MIL-STD-1686C, MIL-HDBK-263). The goal is to keep automation equipment running indefinitely, maximizing customers'' return on investment.', certifications=ARRAY['IPC 7711','IPC 7721','ISO 9001:2000','IEEE','GSA Contractor to T.O. 00-25-234 Standards','MIL-STD-1686C','MIL-HDBK 263']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial electronic repair", "Servomotor repair", "AC/DC drive repair", "Servo drive repair", "Industrial display repair", "Power supply repair", "PLC repair", "ESD and SMT rework", "Component-level repair", "Snapshot reporting", "In-service warranty", "Technical support", "Parts research and inventory management", "5-day repair turnaround", "IPC 7711/7721 certified repair", "ISO 9001:2000 quality system", "GSA contract compliance", "MIL-STD-1686C ESD controls"], "industries": ["Power Companies", "Food Processors", "Oil and Gas Industry", "Chemical Producers", "Industrial Distributors"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["ESD and SMT repair/rework stations"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "5 days for repairs", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["5-day standard repair turnaround", "Pricing 35\u201350% below competitor rates", "Generous warranties on all repairs", "Technicians certified to IPC 7711/7721", "Proactive component-level repair using highest-reliability parts"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 by Walter Bergeron as Synergy Technologies in backyard -> description/db", "Renamed to Power Control Services -> home page", "Located in Broussard, Louisiana -> db", "Industrial electronic repair services -> home page", "Repairs AC/DC drives, servo drives, displays, power supplies, PLCs, servomotors -> home page", "Uses ESD and SMT rework stations -> home page", "5-day repair turnaround -> about page", "Prices 35-50% less than competitors -> about page", "Certifications: IPC 7711, IPC 7721, ISO9001:2000, IEEE, GSA Contractor, MIL-STD-1686C, MIL-HDBK 263 -> about page", "Customers: Entergy, Tyson Foods, Coca Cola, Parker Drilling, NOV, Transocean, Halliburton, Schlumberger, DOW, Conoco Phillips, Disney World -> home page", "Partners with regional and national industrial distributors -> home page", "Mission: ''The Right Way, Right Away'' -> about-us page"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "industrial electronic repair with a \"Price Right\" Guarantee", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/power-control-services/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='power-control-services' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Power Factor is a family-owned solar and electrical contractor headquartered in Baltimore, Maryland. The company was formed in March 2013 by George Lang IV, a master electrician licensed in five states who began his career as an apprentice with Associated Builders and Contractors and later ran the electrical maintenance department at Johns Hopkins Hospital. After designing a Positive Train Control system and a patented battery system for military use at a prior solar firm, Lang brought five key employees with him to launch Power Factor.

The firm provides design, deployment, installation, and maintenance for commercial and residential solar photovoltaic systems, along with general electrical construction, repair, and replacement services. Its capabilities extend to telecommunications infrastructure, LEED-certified lighting retrofits, and electric-vehicle charging station installation. Power Factor employs over 60 people, reports $18 million in annual sales, and has completed more than 2,100 residential installations and over 43 megawatts of solar capacity across the United States and abroad.

Customers include commercial businesses, homeowners, industrial facilities, the U.S. military (including Department of Defense projects), utility companies, and telecommunications providers. The company has delivered over 35 megawatts of projects for defense clients and works with commercial and utility partners nationwide.

Power Factor emphasizes transparent pricing with no hidden fees, 24/7 emergency response, and a workforce that holds NABCEP and OSHA certifications. The founder’s background in military-grade battery systems and the company’s focus on on-time, on-budget delivery reflect its stated mission to provide power to communities through solar and electrical means.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP','OSHA','Maryland Master Electrician License']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial solar PV installation", "Residential solar PV installation", "Electrical maintenance and repair", "Solar PV system design and deployment", "Project management", "LEED-certified lighting retrofits", "EV charging station installation", "Telecommunications infrastructure", "Positive Train Control system design", "Battery energy storage system deployment", "24/7 emergency electrical service", "Permit approvals and compliance"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Residential", "Industrial", "Military/Defense", "Utility", "Telecommunications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["headquarters Baltimore, Maryland -> db", "founded March 2013 -> /about", "founder George Lang IV -> /about", "family-owned -> /about", "over 60 employees -> /about", "$18M annual sales -> /about", "2,100+ residential installations -> /about", "43+ MW solar deployed -> /about", "NABCEP certification -> /about", "OSHA-certified employees -> /about", "BBB A+ rating -> /", "commercial and residential solar services -> /", "telecommunications division, LEED lighting, EV charging -> /about", "work nationally and globally for military -> /about", "no hidden fees, 24/7 emergency -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Power Factor is an electrical and solar company that has been serving the Baltimore area and beyond since 2013.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "over 60", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='power-factor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Power Train Performance, operating as Power Train Plus, is located in Belgrade, Montana, in the Gallatin Valley. It is a two-generation family-owned business, owned and operated by automotive enthusiasts native to the Gallatin Valley.

The shop provides general automotive repair and maintenance, diesel pickup repair for Ford, GM, and Ram platforms, fleet maintenance programs, and performance development services. Its performance division operates a 2,000-hp DynoJet 424X AWD in-ground dyno and a Hunter Hawkeye Elite alignment system capable of handling stock and heavily modified suspensions. The shop also services late-model snowmobiles and side-by-sides, and undertakes full vehicle builds ranging from classic restorations to late-model performance modifications.

Customers include individual vehicle owners from Bozeman, Belgrade, and the broader Gallatin Valley, as well as commercial fleets of various sizes. The shop services daily drivers, work trucks, performance vehicles, and power-sports machines. Reviews highlight service to travelers passing through Yellowstone and local families who have used the shop for generations.

