UPDATE companies SET description='PowerFilm Solar, based in Ames, Iowa, has operated for more than three decades designing and manufacturing custom solar solutions. The company focuses on lightweight, rugged solar panels for transportation, defense, embedded, and specialized applications.

PowerFilm designs and manufactures thin-film amorphous silicon solar panels using proprietary production processes in the United States, and assembles semi-flexible crystalline solar panels domestically. Its in-house capabilities span design engineering, manufacturing, system integration, and electronics integration, including energy harvesting, charge control, and regulated outputs. The company follows a structured development process from requirements definition through prototyping, field testing, and controlled production, with validation through environmental and mechanical testing such as vibration, temperature variation, and long-term outdoor exposure.

The company serves commercial transportation fleets (powering liftgates, telematics, auxiliary power units, and refrigeration), government and Department of Defense programs (portable, vehicle-mounted, and remote field power), uncrewed maritime systems (sealed, marine-exposed platforms), low-speed electric vehicle fleets (campuses, resorts, municipal facilities), Internet of Things deployments (low-power connected devices in remote locations), and consumer markets (mobile, off-grid power). Past projects include telematics, marine, space exploration, and U.S. military applications.

PowerFilm emphasizes application-specific design tailored to program constraints rather than standard product formats, controlled manufacturing with repeatable quality, and direct engineering collaboration with OEM, fleet, and government teams from early design through sustained production. Its U.S.-based manufacturing and prototype-to-production support are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solar panel design engineering", "Thin-film amorphous silicon solar panel manufacturing", "Semi-flexible crystalline solar panel assembly", "System integration (charge controllers, energy harvesting electronics, cabling, mounting)", "Electronics integration (energy harvesting, storage, charge control, regulated outputs)", "Structured development process (requirements, prototyping, field testing, production)", "Design architecture (panel geometry, substrate architecture, encapsulation, electrical interfaces)", "Environmental and mechanical testing (vibration, temperature variation, long-term outdoor exposure)", "Prototype to production manufacturing support", "Quality control and repeatable production processes"], "industries": ["Commercial Transportation", "Government & Defense", "Uncrewed Maritime Systems", "Low-Speed Electric Vehicles", "Internet of Things (IoT)", "Consumer Electronics", "Telematics", "Marine", "Space Exploration"], "materials": ["Amorphous silicon", "Crystalline silicon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Application-specific design tailored to program constraints", "U.S.-based thin-film amorphous silicon manufacturing", "Controlled production with environmental and mechanical validation", "Engineering collaboration from early design through sustained production", "Prototype to production support"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Ames, Iowa -> db", "Operating for more than three decades -> /about-us", "Designs and manufactures thin-film amorphous silicon solar panels in the United States -> /about-us", "Assembles semi-flexible crystalline solar panels in the United States -> /about-us", "Capabilities include design engineering, manufacturing, system integration, electronics integration -> /capabilities", "Serves commercial transportation, government & DoD, uncrewed maritime systems, low-speed electric vehicles, IoT, consumer -> /", "Application-specific design rather than standard product formats -> /about-us", "Controlled manufacturing with environmental and mechanical testing -> /about-us", "Prototype to production support -> /about-us", "Proprietary thin-film production processes -> /about-us", "Success stories include telematics, marine, IoT, United States Military, space exploration -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture thin-film amorphous silicon solar panels in the United States and assemble semi-flexible crystalline solar panels through controlled production processes.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='powerfilm-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Prairie Plastics Holdings operates from Sun Prairie, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1998 as a custom thermoforming specialist. In 2016, Marine Corps veteran Jim Cavezza and manufacturing engineer Jason Zajicek assumed management as managing partners, bringing more than 20 years of industry experience each. Cavezza, honorably discharged as a sergeant after service as a radio field operator from 1999 to 2005, focuses on sales and returnable packaging design, while Zajicek oversees manufacturing, tooling, and quality.

The company provides design, prototyping, single- and twin-sheet thermoforming, CNC trimming, assembly, and kitting. Its product range includes wheel packs, sleeve packs, pallets, returnable packaging, and custom components. Prairie Plastics serves both high-volume and smaller-volume customers, emphasizing an end-to-end approach that covers engineering optimal designs, identifying suitable plastics, establishing efficient development processes, and planning shipping and delivery logistics.

Its model targets buyers who need competitively priced, quality parts without the impersonal experience of larger thermoformers.

Prairie Plastics differentiates itself through a customer-experience mindset: quote responses in hours, project status updates throughout production, and a commitment to have products running within five to six weeks after order acknowledgment. The owners state that serving at the pleasure of both customers and employees drives decisions, aiming to anticipate issues before they become problems and deliver peace of mind alongside the finished part.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom thermoforming", "Design and prototyping", "Single-sheet thermoforming", "Twin-sheet thermoforming", "CNC trimming", "Assembly", "Kitting", "Returnable packaging design", "Material selection consulting", "Shipping and delivery planning"], "industries": ["Thermoforming", "Material handling", "Returnable packaging", "Custom components"], "materials": ["Thermoforming plastics", "Recycled thermoplastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "5-6 weeks after order acknowledged; less than 8 weeks for competitively priced quality parts", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> /about-us", "Located in Sun Prairie, Wisconsin -> /about-us", "Jim Cavezza and Jason Zajicek assumed management in 2016 -> /about-us", "Jim Cavezza honorably discharged Marine Corps sergeant (1999-2005) -> /about-us", "Services: design, prototyping, single- and twin-sheet manufacturing, CNC trim, assembly, kitting -> /about-us", "Products: wheel packs, sleeve packs, pallets, returnable packaging, custom components -> /", "Quote responses in hours -> /", "Product running in 5-6 weeks after order acknowledged -> /", "Project status updates throughout production -> /", "Serves high-volume and smaller-volume customers -> /about-us", "Energy policy mentioned -> /about-us", "Thermoforming plastic recycling mentioned -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in custom thermoform solutions ... single- and twin-sheet manufacturing", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='prairie-plastics-holdings' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business was founded in 2020 when Franklin resident Kyle Dreier purchased the former Welding Unlimited location, retaining much of its equipment and workforce. The company is structured as a locally owned and operated limited liability company.

The shop focuses on structural steel fabrication and installation, producing columns, beams, brackets, flitch plates, stairs, and bollards for commercial and residential projects. It also builds custom metalwork such as wrought‑iron handrails for stairs, balconies, and porches; steel and wrought‑iron gates for security and decorative purposes; and handles welding repairs on heavy equipment, skid‑steer attachments, and dump‑truck beds. Additional services include trailer repair and modification (fenders, ramps, wiring, axle replacements) and hitch installation for buses and trucks. The crew describes itself as medium‑sized, with many fabricators and welders who have been at the facility for more than 15 years, bringing decades of combined experience.

Prather Metalworks serves two primary customer groups: contractors and builders who need structural steel and fabrication delivered on schedule, and homeowners seeking handrails, gates, or repair work with responsive communication. Commercial clients include projects requiring entrance gates, bollards, and custom fabrication such as delivery boxes, assembly‑line carts, chimney caps, and firewood racks. The company also works with heavy‑equipment operators and trailer owners across Middle Tennessee.

The company emphasizes upfront pricing and communication. It provides quotes before any work begins and commits to honoring those quotes even if a job proves more involved than expected. A stated policy promises a return call within 24 hours of an inquiry, and the owner highlights quality and communication as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Structural steel installation", "Custom metal fabrication", "Welding repair", "Handrail fabrication", "Handrail installation", "Gate fabrication", "Gate installation", "Trailer repair", "Trailer modification", "Bus and truck hitch installation", "Custom metal fabrication (delivery boxes, carts, chimney caps, firewood racks)", "Design, fabrication, installation"], "industries": ["Contractors and Builders", "Homeowners", "Commercial", "Residential", "Heavy equipment", "Trailer", "Bus and Truck"], "materials": ["Structural steel", "Wrought iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quotes provided before commitment", "Commitment to quoted price even if job overruns", "24-hour callback promise", "Crew with decades of experience", "Locally owned and operated"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 by Kyle Dreier -> /about", "Located at 120 Confederate Drive, Franklin, TN -> /", "Locally owned and operated -> /", "Medium-sized metal fabrication company -> /", "Services: structural steel fabrication, handrails, welding repair, gates, trailer repair, bus/truck hitches -> /services", "Customer types: contractors, builders, homeowners -> /", "Quotes before commitment, stick to quotes -> /about", "24-hour callback promise -> /", "Crew with decades of experience -> /about", "Materials: structural steel, wrought iron -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''re a locally owned and operated metal fabrication shop in Franklin, Tennessee.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='prather-metalworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pravi Apparel operates a U.S. sales office in Lancaster, Pennsylvania, while its manufacturing facility, known as Praville, is located in Haiti. Production began in January 2021 after founder Jim Weber built a solar‑powered plant in a town without running water or electricity. The venture started with a mission to create jobs and pull people out of poverty in Haiti, employing individuals like Elyse Ledix, who joined the team after being widowed.

The company produces only polo shirts, offered in four lines—Biz‑Wear, Pravi‑Golf, Wear‑Strong, and Dura‑Text. All shirts are assembled in Haiti using 100 % American‑made fabrics and feature a self‑fabric collar typically found in higher‑priced apparel. The solar‑powered factory has a capacity of up to 275 workers.

Pravi targets buyers of industrial‑strength uniform polos, golf polos, and workwear. Its shirts are marketed to businesses seeking durable, comfortable uniforms and to consumers looking for performance golf or casual wear.

Pravi’s differentiator is its social mission: for every 4,000 shirts sold, the company says it pulls one Haitian out of poverty. It keeps prices low by avoiding rent, property taxes, utilities, and tariffs, and by using interest‑free loans with no repayment timeline.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polo shirt manufacturing", "Apparel assembly", "Fabric sourcing (100% American-made)", "Self-fabric collar construction", "Solar-powered production facility"], "industries": ["Uniform apparel", "Golf apparel", "Workwear", "Industrial uniforms"], "materials": ["100% American-made fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only company offering industrial\u2011strength uniform polos that combat poverty", "100\u202f% American\u2011made fabrics assembled in Haiti", "Self\u2011fabric collar for comfort", "Solar\u2011powered plant in Haiti with capacity for 275 employees", "No rent, property taxes, utilities, or tariffs; interest\u2011free loans"], "facts_used": ["Production began January 2021 -> /about", "Factory in Praville, Haiti; US sales office in Lancaster, PA -> /about", "Founder Jim Weber built solar-powered plant -> /about", "Employee Elyse Ledix joined after being widowed -> /about", "Only makes polo shirts, four lines -> /about", "Shirts assembled in Haiti with 100% American-made fabrics -> /about", "Self-fabric collar feature -> /about", "Plant capacity up to 275 employees -> /about", "Mission: for every 4000 shirts sold, pull a Haitian out of poverty -> /about, /", "Low prices due to no rent, taxes, utilities, tariffs, interest-free loans -> /about", "Industries: uniform polos, golf polos, workwear -> /", "Headquarters city/state from db -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We only make polo shirts! That is our sole focus.", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "Up to 275", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "lang