UPDATE companies SET description='Priority Plastics Inc. is headquartered in Grand Prairie, Texas, and operates extrusion blow‑molding facilities across the United States. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, and no founders are named in public materials.

The company manufactures plastic packaging solutions including HDPE and PET containers, tight‑head pails, canisters, and dry‑pack towel wipes. Core processes are extrusion blow molding and injection stretch blow molding (ISBM), the latter marketed as a way to expand PET applications. A multi‑plant footprint enables coast‑to‑coast production, multi‑plant sourcing, and in‑plant customer‑service support. The firm also develops custom tooling and maintains an expanding library of stock tools to shorten lead times.

Priority Plastics serves customers ranging from startups to multinational firms in food and beverage, nutrition and wellness, industrial, personal care, agriculture, animal health, cannabis/hemp/CBD, hardware, hazardous materials, healthcare/nutraceuticals, and specialty chemicals.

The company emphasizes four pillars—quality, timeliness, relationships, and sustainability. Its GreenLite platform incorporates post‑consumer recycled (PCR) content and lightweight designs; the PriorityPour ECO line uses up to 80 % recycled core material. Public targets include sourcing 60 % of materials from recycled or renewable sources by 2035, making 80 % of products recyclable by 2028, and cutting Scope 2 and 3 emissions 30 % by 2030. All facilities recycle unused resin, and the geographically distributed network is positioned to lower freight costs and carbon emissions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion blow molding", "Injection stretch blow molding (ISBM)", "Custom tooling design and modification", "In-plant customer service support", "Multi-plant sourcing", "Labeling capabilities", "PriorityONE technical capability", "The Cyclone process", "Sustainable packaging design (GreenLite)", "PCR material incorporation"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Nutrition & Wellness", "Industrial", "Personal Care", "Agriculture", "Animal Health", "Cannabis/Hemp/CBD", "Hardware", "Hazardous materials", "Healthcare/Nutra", "Specialty Chemicals"], "materials": ["HDPE", "PET", "Post-consumer recycled (PCR) materials", "Recycled core materials (up to 80% in ECO Multi-Layer)"], "equipment": ["Injection stretch blow molding machines", "Extrusion blow molding machines", "The Cyclone", "PriorityONE system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Coast-to-coast manufacturing footprint lowering freight costs", "Multi-plant sourcing capability", "In-plant customer service support", "Custom tooling development and expanded stock tool library", "GreenLite sustainability platform with PCR materials and recycled-content targets"], "facts_used": ["HQ Grand Prairie Texas -> db", "extrusion blow-molding manufacturing facilities throughout US -> /", "Injection Stretch Blow Molding capabilities -> /", "HDPE containers, PET containe