UPDATE companies SET description='Pro AG Equipment traces its roots to 1948 when Lockwood Corp. was established in Grand Forks, North Dakota. The business transitioned to its current name, Pro Ag Equipment, in 1982. Headquartered in Grafton, North Dakota, the company operates three locations: Grand Forks and Grafton in North Dakota, and Hastings in Florida.

The company functions primarily as a distributor of short-line equipment tailored for sugar beet, bean, and potato farming. Beyond new equipment sales, Pro Ag Equipment supplies parts, liquid fertilizer components, and provides repair services.

Pro Ag Equipment serves growers and agricultural operations specializing in sugar beet, bean, and potato production.

